// The approval gate written against the COMPLETED approval -- the strong form.
//
// A trade needs an approval that actually went through, earlier in the same session. AgentCore
// records a denied action as an `::error` event rather than a `::response`, so a run of refused
// approvals leaves this gate shut and the trade is refused with it.
//
// Compare approval_gate_request.dw. That file is this one with a single word changed and it has
// the opposite security property. The pair is the finding; neither half means much alone.
//
// Judged by the real engine in tests/strands/dogwood_replay.py, because Dogwood's own regression
// corpus contains no `::error` in any of its 521 cases and so cannot answer this.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Anchor::Action::"Trade",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    formerly within 1000s Anchor::Action::"Approve"::response{ }
};
